# Everything here is either a shell script, a Python script or a systemd unit,
# and all of it is checked out onto a Pi, where a CRLF shebang fails as
# "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M". The blobs are already LF - they were authored
# on Windows with core.autocrlf enabled, which normalises on commit - but that
# depends on the contributor's local setting. Pinning it here makes the
# repository's line endings a property of the repository instead.
* text=auto eol=lf
